# Git Operations Rules

## Commit and Push Requirements
- **ALL** git commits **SHALL** be followed by a `git push`
- Never commit without pushing
- Ensure all changes are properly synchronized with remote repository

## Commit Message Format
- Include detailed technical attribution comment at the top of each commit message
- Format:
```
/**
 * This code written by Claude Sonnet 4 (claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022)
 * Generated via Cursor IDE (cursor.sh) with AI assistance
 * Model: Anthropic Claude 3.5 Sonnet
 * Generation timestamp: {{timestamp}}
 * Context: {{brief_description_of_what_this_code_does}}
 * 
 * Technical details:
 * - LLM: Claude 3.5 Sonnet (2024-10-22)
 * - IDE: Cursor (cursor.sh)
 * - Generation method: AI-assisted pair programming
 * - Code style: {{language_specific_style_guide}}
 * - Dependencies: {{key_dependencies}}
 */
```

## Git User Configuration
- Change git user to "<user> | Cursor.sh | <model>" before committing
- This identifies automated commits from AI assistance
